  "feel": [
    {
      "topic": "Exact numbers (SG-33)",
      "rule": "`SangamValueMapper` maps FEEL numbers to `Long` when whole, otherwise to `BigDecimal`, never to `Double`. `BigDecimal` and `Money` (exact major amount) go in unchanged. `typeRef=\"number\"` is registered as an exact type (`NumberDataTypeTransformer`)."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Money types at deploy (SG-33, R44)",
      "rule": "A `.dmn` input, output or variable with `typeRef=\"double\"`/`\"float\"` whose name, label or expression is money (amount, value, cost, fee, limit, budget, price, charge, …) is **refused**. Other doubles get a warning recommending `number`. Money uses `long` (minor units) or `number`. All 176 shipped pack files were migrated from `double` to `number`, so no justified doubles remain."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Strict evaluation (SG-34)",
      "rule": "A FEEL failure or suppressed failure fails the decision with `SANGAM-FEEL-STRICT`. This covers a missing variable, a null or mistyped operand, division by zero, an unknown function, an invalid literal date/time/duration/number, and a null condition. Native FEEL would return null, take the else branch, or fire a catch-all rule. A value that is genuinely null is still a value: `x = null` and `x != null` work."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Null decision-table input (SG-34)",
      "rule": "A null input is an error (`SANGAM-DMN-NULL-INPUT`) unless at least one rule tests that input with `null`. A catch-all `-` never catches a null. With an explicit null rule, a null input matches only the null tests."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Failure handling",
      "rule": "The check runs inside the engine command, before the result reaches the process. No rule's output is used and the command rolls back. On an async business rule task the result is an incident on the task. After the data is corrected, a job retry evaluates again and resolves the incident."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Date-time equality (SG-35)",
      "rule": "DMN 1.3 compares date-times on the time line (OMG issue DMN13-35, resolved in DMN 1.3: `=` is the same instant). The pinned engine's `=` also compares the zone (feel-scala issue #767), and an operator cannot be overridden without changing the engine, which the SG-27 pin forbids. **Policy: the spec semantics, same instant.** Until the engine is upgraded, the deploy-time lint `SANGAM-DMN-DATETIME-EQ` warns on `=`/`!=`, and on a bare input entry, against a zoned date-time literal. Models compare instants with `<`, `>`, ranges, or `a - b = duration(\"PT0S\")`. This is a documented gap, not a silent rule."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Known residual",
      "rule": "A built-in conversion (`date(x)`, `duration(x)`, …) whose argument is a **variable** holding an invalid string still yields null in the pinned engine (built-ins cannot be overridden). Literal arguments are refused. A null that reaches a later operator, a decision-table input or a required output is still caught (strict evaluation, null-input rule, R10 `requiredOutputs`)."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Status",
      "rule": "Decision: DECIDED (SG-33/34/35 root-cause fixes, 2026-11-08). Delivery: IMPLEMENTED (`sangam-engine` `org.sangam.engine.feel`). Tests: `FeelBehaviourH2Test`, `DmnModelLintTest`."
    }
  ]
